#!/bin/sh
# Enforces CLAUDE.md § 6: the two review passes run before anything is pushed.
#
# This lives in git rather than in a Claude Code hook so that it applies to
# whoever pushes — any agent, any session, a human at a terminal. Activated by
# core.hooksPath, set by the `prepare` script on install; see KNOWN_ISSUES.md.
#
# The marker is bound to a commit sha: a new commit invalidates it, so passes
# run early in a session cannot vouch for work done after them.

marker=$(git rev-parse --git-path review-passed)
reviewed=$(cat "$marker" 2>/dev/null)

# git feeds one line per ref being pushed: <local ref> <local sha> <remote ref> <remote sha>
while read -r _local_ref local_sha _remote_ref _remote_sha; do
  # A deletion pushes the null sha — there is nothing to review.
  case "$local_sha" in *[!0]*) ;; *) continue ;; esac
  [ "$local_sha" = "$reviewed" ] && continue

  cat >&2 <<MSG

Blocked by .githooks/pre-push — CLAUDE.md § 6.

Two review passes are required on the commit being pushed:

  1. /simplify        quality pass, on the working tree, before committing
                      (or your agent's equivalent review)
  2. /security-review  after committing — it reads commits, not the tree

Act on what they find, then record the reviewed commit and push again:

  pnpm review:ok

  pushing:  $local_sha
  recorded: ${reviewed:-none}

Deliberate exception (documentation typo, revert, hotfix): git push --no-verify
MSG
  exit 1
done

exit 0
